-# Repository work: Research Autopilot Work Harness
+# Research Autopilot — direct research edition
 
-The owner selects one experiment program at a time and descending supported
-batches (e.g. 64, 32, 16, 8, 4, 2). Apply single-experiment-batching.md on the actual
-execution target, preserve scientific batch semantics, and keep Chat CPU/4 GB.
+The owner retired mandatory Work Harness orchestration and requested prompt-guided B/C/D/E. The active policy is `skills/research-autopilot/SKILL.md` and its four `prompt-*.md` phase guides. Historical source/controller docs are implementation history, not execution instructions. Do not introduce mandatory schemas, per-command review, stage gates or micro-workers.
 
-The owner explicitly authorizes the fifth Work-derived edition, autonomous-rsi-harness,
-in addition to main, autonomous-rsi, autonomous-rsi-chat and rsi-simple. This fifth
-source branch is authorized and supersedes inherited four-branch restrictions.
-Preserve the existing four branches. Keep Codex and other existing local agents;
-borrow DeepSeek Harness mechanisms without installing or replacing the agent backend.
-Main is Web GPT + local agent with human scientific decisions; Work, Work Harness
-and Simple use local agents; Chat uses ChatGPT
-Chat CPU tools under a 4 GB RAM planning ceiling. All deepen one selected field.
-The local agent is the user's control/supervision point, not a local-only compute
-restriction. First restore/check existing authorized SSH GPU targets; sync pinned
-code, submit and monitor jobs on the actual target and collect real results.
-No Docker on any host or edition, including scoring; use native environments.
-Restore actual deferred-scoring support before applying scorer requirements to
-training. Block only genuine stage dependencies; preserve unscored artifacts. This maintenance edits
-source guidance and does not connect to a GPU server, launch research or migrate
-installed/pinned projects. Chat keeps its CPU/4 GB execution profile.
-Read edition-policy.md, research-harness.md, research-cycle.md and round-continuation.md first.
-This edition adds a persistent research program, whole-goal coverage, real command
-planner/reviewer invocations, native tasks and result archiving/recovery.
-The skills-only ZIP does not install the source runtime. No default service setup
-or live unattended qualification is implied. Respect explicit pause in durable
-program state even when the conversation host has no active goal object.
-Preserve plugin identity, sharing, live source pins and existing research tasks.
-
-The current source update applies program-owned ordered execution of the existing
-84-node Autopilot Skill. Read docs/SKILL_SEQUENCE.md and skill-sequence.md.
-The planner compatibility role performs the current step; code alone advances,
-repeats or finishes after per-step evidence and independent acceptance. New
-contracts use schema 2; old contracts are exact recovery only. Optional scopes
-follow the user objective and do not add publication authority. This source task
-does not add/run tests, models, SSH workloads or live-project adoption.
-
-Use GitHub only for direct file/Git-data pull and push. Do not use Actions,
-workflow runs, workflow dispatch, CI control APIs or publication/PR branches.
-Run required checks and package builds on the authorized host, then publish each
-edition using its own expected parent and exact-content readback. Keep
-`.github/workflows` absent in all five branches; do not recreate workflow files.
-Record execution on the actual host in plain log files, then push the reviewed
-logs to GitHub as ordinary files with their source revision and exit status.
-Use `logs/maintenance/` for this repository's maintenance logs. Do not upload
-credentials or private environment values. Do not use Actions artifacts or run
-records as the log store. Repository Actions is disabled; do not re-enable it.
-This source maintenance does not migrate pinned scheduled tasks or change another
-research repository.
-If GitHub read/write/readback is unavailable, follow
-`skills/research-autopilot/references/github-zip-fallback.md`: preserve the actual
-work and logs in a verified downloadable ZIP, and mark remote sync pending/unknown.
-
-Use the actual authorized host and available tools. Preserve scientific evidence,
-native protocols, independent review, failed findings, cumulative budgets, pauses
-and pinned live attempts. Never invent scheduler activation or scientific success.
-Use host subagents for useful independent review and skill behavior validation,
-with disjoint writes and one integration/publishing writer.
-
-This is repository source maintenance, not an installed personal-skill update or
-authorization to resume a research project. Publish each selected edition using
-expected-parent update and exact readback. Preserve other contributors' changes.
-Before research-program work, read docs/RESEARCH_PROGRAM.md,
-docs/architecture/research-program.md and docs/COMMAND_AGENT.md. The inherited
-docs/architecture/runtime-spec.md, docs/RUNTIME.md and docs/LOCAL_AGENT_RUNBOOK.md
-describe underlying or optional backends; their backend-specific prerequisites
-do not automatically apply to independent source reading and preparation.
-
-For a later user-requested verification task, use meaningful behavior checks.
-The inherited integration commands are:
-
-```bash
-PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/runtime -p 'test_*.py' -q
-PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s skills/research-autopilot/tests -p 'test_*.py' -q
-PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/plugins -p 'test_*.py' -q
-python3 scripts/refresh_edition_export.py --base-revision OBSERVED_PARENT_SHA
-python3 skills/research-autopilot/scripts/research_nodes.py check
-git diff --check
-```
-
-Never commit runtime databases, caches, credentials or fabricated experiment
-evidence. Source publication, package validation, installation, project adoption
-and live unattended execution must be reported separately.
-
-## Current owner instruction: sustained phase execution
-
-The owner explicitly requests implementing/installing phase-sized Work Harness
-autonomy before resuming SPECTRUM research. This supersedes inherited per-node
-transport and source-only/no-adoption instructions for this update. Preserve all
-evidence duties, independent phase/scientific review and actual GPU execution.
-Code tests run on the authorized hn01 GPU host. Parent is the sole integration
-writer; use independent review without splitting research into micro-agents.
+Preserve the plugin identity and other editions. Retain legacy runtime/source and evidence for recovery; do not reactivate old controllers. Use the existing authorized GPU for code tests/experiments when requested, never report tests or scientific results that were not run. Keep credentials out of Git. Scientific rigor is expressed in the phase guidance and actual analyses, not admission machinery.
