+---
+name: research-autopilot
+description: "Use for sustained one-field research with existing local agents executing and accepting the existing Autopilot Skill in program-owned order."
+---
+
+# Research Autopilot
+
+## Living project memory and GPU-aware design
+
+At A intake create the [living project handbook](references/project-handbook-and-gpu-design.md); B/C/D/E read and update it with motivation, gap, idea, mathematics, experiment design, hardware profiles and actual evidence. Bootstrap ongoing projects from existing records. Design scientifically meaningful experiments together with feasible GPU execution, using measured descending batch probes and preserving scientific hyperparameters.
+
+## Question-led research selection
+
+Read [question-led experiment selection](references/question-led-experiment-selection.md) for B memory, C diagnosis, D mechanism development and E coverage. Reassess inherited hypotheses and choose informative models/data/conditions before reusing assets; old setup, cache and prior acceptance do not settle scientific fit. Worker and reviewer apply this within the existing phase, without another gate or model-size quota.
+
+## Official code and adaptive GPU execution
+
+Read [official code and adaptive GPU execution](references/gpu-adaptive-execution.md) for every experimental stage. Reuse official code and the authorized GPU; install, adapt, debug and execute inside the sustained worker. Missing scorer integration is owned repair work, and blocks only work that consumes its scores.
+
+## Sustained phase mode (Work Harness)
+
+Harness guides research logic, memory and phase acceptance. Give the sustained
+worker freedom to revise methods, implementation and experimental details from
+actual GPU debugging/results. Initial plans are hypotheses; record real execution
+and changes. Routine preparation/debug/development needs no per-call formal E
+experiment review. Genuine dependency blocks retain a nonterminal checkpoint;
+unchanged errors must not spawn repeated workers.
+
+For `sequence.execution_mode: phase_autonomy`, read [sustained phase execution](references/phase-autonomy.md).
+This mode overrides inherited per-node/per-edit worker handoffs: one sustained
+worker performs the phase's reading, mathematics, code, GPU experiments and debug;
+all milestone evidence is reviewed together at the phase boundary. C requires
+core-paper official code, task-relevant strong methods and checked community
+implementation leads through the explicit `C.method_basis` requirement. Ordinary
+B02/B03/B04 work retrieves B's shared research memory first, refreshes missing
+paper/code/community evidence through B, then returns to C's mathematical and
+experimental question. Results determine advancement, experiment revision or
+problem reselection; write findings and failures back into memory. Ordinary
+B/C/D research iterations stay within the worker; accepted scientific gates use
+typed revisits. B05/M05 and formal E/freeze remain substantive acceptance points.
