+## Execute and accept the existing Skill in program order
+
+Read [skill-sequence.md](references/skill-sequence.md) before any program task.
+The program owns the canonical 84-node order, current step, acceptance and
+repeat/once behavior. The `planner` transport role is the current-step worker;
+it cannot choose a successor, skip a step or end the goal. Read the assigned node,
+perform its work, bind fixed requirements to real evidence, read back child-task
+results, and obtain separate review before code advances the cursor. Every node
+is represented; only program rules can mark user-unrequested optional scopes
+inactive. This ordering rule governs inherited next-action wording below.
+
+The scientific method is unchanged: deepen one field through papers/code,
+purposeful reproduction, concrete questions, mathematical modeling as needed,
+credible benchmarks and strong baselines, actual results and knowledge updates.
+New program contracts use schema 2 with mandatory research scope. Manuscript,
+revision, release and communication scopes require the actual user objective;
+source updates do not authorize extra publication or migrate existing programs.
