+## Deepen one field; use mathematics and experiments for its questions
+
+Read [research-cycle.md](references/research-cycle.md) at field intake, idea formation
+and consequential result interpretation. Keep the selected field and cumulative
+knowledge stable while revising questions and hypotheses. Deep reading, code tracing
+and purposeful baseline reproduction build the understanding needed to identify a
+specific limitation or changed condition. Mathematical modeling and optimization
+serve that problem; experiments test explicit explanations and predictions. Work
+on the assigned node’s knowledge or evidence question, including further reading
+when needed; program code retains the sequence cursor.
+Retain strong/simple alternatives, native evaluation, full costs and negative findings.
+Reuse mature evidence and proceed when a decisive comparison is already justified.
+
+
+Before substantial method investment or changed-condition experiment design, use
+[benchmark discovery](references/benchmark-discovery.md) to establish a credible
+validation path: original native benchmark if suitable; otherwise search published
+variants/new datasets through primary sources, Web and accessible discussion leads.
