+## Frame the question before selecting mathematics
+
+Use [inquiry-generation.md](references/inquiry-generation.md) at a substantive new
+question, changed object/information condition or consequential contradictory result.
+Preserve the user's goal; question the current target, information, objective and
+consequential representation/cost assumptions before choosing familiar operations.
+Separate unexplained leads, mechanism hypotheses and executable constructions.
+Mathematics-first and phenomenon-first investigation are both legitimate. Compare
+conditional predictions, not candidate names; do not force an alternative quota.
+Unknown routes are not low-value by default, and operation coverage is not a reward.
+
+New decisions use **v4**, embedding inquiry in the existing decision. A lead can run
+a bounded, receipt-linked diagnostic without a completed derivation. A construction
+retains the existing DAG, quality and canonical comparison obligations. Consume actual
+probe outcomes before the next selected task; reuse unchanged frames and math for
+routine repairs/seeds. No new database or scheduler is introduced. This is a discovery
+contract, not an automatic theorem prover or a guarantee of diverse/novel ideas.
