+## Essential scientific obligations
+
+- Join primary papers/full text, actual implementations and established benchmark
+  protocols. Before empirical design, read
+  [paper-grounded experiment design](references/paper-grounded-experiment-design.md):
+  extract published experiments from main text, appendix and code/configs, then
+  justify which practices to adopt, adapt or reject for the actual claims.
+  Recheck changed dependencies; reuse unchanged pinned reads.
+- Default to one hypothesis per iteration. Retain a consequential derivation,
+  assumptions, constructed rule, prediction, falsifier and independent review.
+  The canonical batch uses pool_target=1 and selection_target=1 with the explicit
+  edition target_override described in chat-execution.md. Broader discovery is
+  an intentional mode, not a prerequisite for every repair.
+- Before substantial candidate investment, inspect closest primary work, the
+  qualified strongest simple alternative, value, mechanism and falsifier. Track
+  hypothesis families and retire refuted or redundant mechanisms. Cheap parallel
+  investigation of competing explanations need not create multiple expensive
+  candidate campaigns.
+- Obtain missing baseline/resource/scorer evidence through feasible preflight
+  work. Require applicable Parent/Gate 0/IPCG and method evidence before investing
+  in a new candidate; missing evidence generates an acquisition/check task.
+- Preserve published native data, splits, labels, metrics and scoring for native
+  benchmark claims. Development diagnostics and engineering tests are allowed
+  for their stated purpose; they cannot substitute for scientific comparisons.
+- Write complete designs for the requested scope, including comparisons,
+  controls, uncertainty, resource assumptions and reproducible commands. Keep
+  a claim-to-experiment contract whose required coverage survives finite batches.
+  Use observed authorized compute and measured calibration; historical GPU
+  ownership is not current access. Keep development separate from frozen
+  confirmation. Do not tune on confirmation.
+- Run available authorized checks on the current host. Retain real output and
+  error records. Apply E04 and independent verification before scientific
+  conclusions. Authored, executed, scoped-supported and final-claim states differ.
+- Route failures by cause: environment/configuration to setup; implementation to
+  repair; evidence gaps to collection/review. For valid counterevidence identify
+  the claim and conditions actually refuted; supply the current node’s required
+  reading, reproduction, diagnosis or revision evidence. Retain justified successor
+  hypotheses without moving the cursor. A candidate KILL preserves the research
+  goal and history. Explicit user/project stop remains terminal; other admitted
+  child work for the same node may continue.
+- Program code owns cycle/goal closure under repeat/once semantics, with required
+  evidence and delivery receipts. No-gap or a positive review alone is not proof
+  of acceptance or complete delivery.
+  Writing states the scope and limitations of actual evidence.
+
+Read [method-verification.md](references/method-verification.md),
+[full validation](references/full-validation-and-review.md),
+[development](references/development-and-execution.md),
+[Gate A](references/gate-a.md), [native evaluation](references/native-evaluation.md)
+and [claims](references/statistics-and-claims.md) at their relevant boundaries.
