-Separate the project goal from the current milestone. Use research mode for
-authorized continuing inquiry; CPU feasibility or paper selection then remains
-a prerequisite. Use bounded_task for an explicitly scoped selection, reproduction,
-audit or artifact request; loading this skill does not expand that scope. Do not
-replace a broader research request with an easier milestone and call it completed.
-Use the goal contract and completion review in chat-execution.md. Count actual
-runs separately from scientific cycles; one candidate at a time is not one round
-per goal. Resume the original cumulative limits rather than inventing a new quota.
-
-For a new project, reuse supplied targets and infer routine reversible choices
-from the task. A missing optional HF target or route label must not block useful
-investigation. Resolve only concrete missing authority, access or scope choices.
-Record finite working limits; do not repeatedly ask for already supplied approval.
-Use [workflow-harness.md](references/workflow-harness.md) for the assigned action and
-[research-policy.md](references/research-policy.md) only for applicable details.
-
-## Project cooperation barrier
-
-Apply project-cooperation.md when actual independent participants concurrently
-share a project. Restore the authorized registry, observe relevant evidence,
-claim jobs conditionally and reconcile unknown writes before retry. A solitary
-local agent needs no cloud registry. Same-workspace children use disjoint paths
-and one integration owner; main's sequential human-mediated handoff uses concrete
-packets. Never invent peers, scan unrelated conversations or duplicate a live job.
-Keep source pins, cumulative budgets and pauses through every handoff.
-
-## Essential scientific obligations
-
-- Join primary papers/full text, actual implementations and established benchmark
-  protocols. Before empirical design, read
-  [paper-grounded experiment design](references/paper-grounded-experiment-design.md):
-  extract published experiments from main text, appendix and code/configs, then
-  justify which practices to adopt, adapt or reject for the actual claims.
-  Recheck changed dependencies; reuse unchanged pinned reads.
-- Default to one hypothesis per iteration. Retain a consequential derivation,
-  assumptions, constructed rule, prediction, falsifier and independent review.
-  The canonical batch uses pool_target=1 and selection_target=1 with the explicit
-  edition target_override described in chat-execution.md. Broader discovery is
-  an intentional mode, not a prerequisite for every repair.
-- Before substantial candidate investment, inspect closest primary work, the
-  qualified strongest simple alternative, value, mechanism and falsifier. Track
-  hypothesis families and retire refuted or redundant mechanisms. Cheap parallel
-  investigation of competing explanations need not create multiple expensive
-  candidate campaigns.
-- Obtain missing baseline/resource/scorer evidence through feasible preflight
-  work. Require applicable Parent/Gate 0/IPCG and method evidence before investing
-  in a new candidate; missing evidence generates an acquisition/check task.
-- Preserve published native data, splits, labels, metrics and scoring for native
-  benchmark claims. Development diagnostics and engineering tests are allowed
-  for their stated purpose; they cannot substitute for scientific comparisons.
-- Write complete designs for the requested scope, including comparisons,
-  controls, uncertainty, resource assumptions and reproducible commands. Keep
-  a claim-to-experiment contract whose required coverage survives finite batches.
-  Use observed authorized compute and measured calibration; historical GPU
-  ownership is not current access. Keep development separate from frozen
-  confirmation. Do not tune on confirmation.
-- Run available authorized checks on the current host. Retain real output and
-  error records. Apply E04 and independent verification before scientific
-  conclusions. Authored, executed, scoped-supported and final-claim states differ.
-- Route failures by cause: environment/configuration to setup; implementation to
-  repair; evidence gaps to collection/review. For valid counterevidence identify
-  the claim and conditions actually refuted; supply the current node’s required
-  reading, reproduction, diagnosis or revision evidence. Retain justified successor
-  hypotheses without moving the cursor. A candidate KILL preserves the research
-  goal and history. Explicit user/project stop remains terminal; other admitted
-  child work for the same node may continue.
-- Program code owns cycle/goal closure under repeat/once semantics, with required
-  evidence and delivery receipts. No-gap or a positive review alone is not proof
-  of acceptance or complete delivery.
-  Writing states the scope and limitations of actual evidence.
-
-Read [method-verification.md](references/method-verification.md),
-[full validation](references/full-validation-and-review.md),
-[development](references/development-and-execution.md),
-[Gate A](references/gate-a.md), [native evaluation](references/native-evaluation.md)
-and [claims](references/statistics-and-claims.md) at their relevant boundaries.
-
-## Roles and actual execution
-
-Proposal, review and control are separate responsibilities on the actual host,
-not mandatory separate computers. Use genuine independent review tasks when
-available. A missing reviewer leaves affected acceptance pending and does not
-block unrelated work. A second self-authored success sentence is not verification.
-Give reviewers frozen evidence and acceptance criteria without the author's
-expected verdict. Parallel readers, disjoint writers and reviewers retain their
-actual identities; only the coordinator integrates and publishes. Child completion
-is not a scientific pass or a reason to end the research loop.
-
-Restore the authorized execution target and inspect its actual compute, data,
-runtime and budget. The local control agent submits feasible commands on that
-target and collects measured evidence; its own computer is not the default GPU host. Use no Docker
-and assume no GPU or paid model service. Missing capabilities remain explicit.
-The generated_unexecuted label applies only while an artifact is actually
-unexecuted, not permanently to everything produced through a Web interface.
-
-Restore existing SSH/runbook choices at startup; reuse already authorized targets.
-Read full-runtime setup only when that particular runtime is selected.
-Do not require Local handoff files for a host-contained project. Do not relabel a
-scientific workload as maintenance to evade evidence requirements.
-
-## Runtime library and recovery
-
-For strategy migration, invocation reads, durable manifests and command receipts,
-read [Chat control records](references/chat-control-records.md). New research
-dispatch uses sourced decisions and current invocation observations; legacy
-settlement and explicit user pauses remain intact.
-
-The local agent controls the active loop and supervises jobs on their selected
-local or authorized SSH execution targets. This fifth edition's managed loop
-uses its separately installed research-program runtime; read
-[research-harness.md](references/research-harness.md). Existing command agents
-need no ACP adapter. Read [runtime-library.md](references/runtime-library.md)
-when configuring the underlying controller or optional ACP/native backend.
-
-Persist coherent artifacts and source-bound checkpoints at milestones and before
-yielding; use scripts/chat_cycle.py when available for revision-checked action
-bookkeeping. Select work by outstanding goal obligations and expected decision
-value; bound diagnostics and review stagnation using
-[research decisions](references/chat-research-decisions.md). Use advance to obtain
-the actual pinned procedure text and action,
-then execute it with real host tools, optionally dividing independent work into
-bounded child packets under that parent attempt. Reconcile and integrate the wave
-before recording the parent result and calling advance again in the same active
-turn; no user confirmation is needed for routine in-scope continuation. See
-chat-cycle-records.md for parallel events, classified repair and versioned outputs.
-The helper is neither a scheduler nor a scientific verifier. Restore unfinished
-attempts and exact partial work on continuation; do not restart from a summary.
-
-Keep failures, cumulative budgets and stable side-effect identities. Reconcile
-lost acknowledgements before retrying. Repair dependent tasks against the real
-replacement outputs; never turn an old failure into a pass or mutate live pins.
-Accept a procedure update only after fixed checks and review, persist/read its
-version for the next round, and preserve rollback. Installed plugins and running
-attempts are not silently updated by a project-local procedure change.
-
-## Navigation and delivery
-
-The [node index](references/node-index.md) remains 84 tasks, 16 regions and 221
-conditional relationships. They are navigation, not a mandatory execution DAG,
-new scientific gates or authorization. Load selected exact bound sections with
-`python3 "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/research_nodes.py" show NODE_ID`; `check` validates
-source/graph integrity only. Runtime queues schedule actual finite dependencies.
-
-For authorized Web GitHub code/design delivery, use the selected project's delegated
-target branch, one integration writer, current expected-parent update and exact commit/
-file readback; preserve others' work and pinned running workspaces. Return actual
-repo/commit/packet paths. Local returns raw receipts/results, E04 and continuation/
-budget gaps for Web review; fetch the supervisor-admitted next revision without
-changing live attempts or repeating completed work. Reuse startup destinations
-and scoped connections; report unavailable reads/writes honestly.
-
-STOP, NO NEW IDEA NEEDED, REPAIR EVIDENCE and RETARGET WRITING are valid. Retain
-next action on pause. Before retrying any external operation reconcile its real
-provider ID; without queryable identity/idempotency after lost acknowledgment,
-report the blocker. Do not auto-install dependencies, launch paid compute,
-fabricate approvals/receipts or treat local records as a shared-host upload.
-
-## Progress observations
-
-At project start/resume, meaningful task/stage changes, blockers, handoffs and
-before yielding, follow [progress-observability](references/progress-observability.md).
-Keep task descriptions, responsible actor, observed timestamps, blocker and next
-action; export the existing Local controller read-only. Observer failures warn
-without blocking research. This adds no gate, verdict, background activity or
-permission; the selected edition still owns execution and step-7 decisions.
-Track coverage, qualified baselines, critical dependencies, hypothesis evidence,
-review and delivery separately from run counts. Retain valid negative progress;
-do not reward repeated nearby experiments or call a stage number a research cycle.
-
-Operational anomalies require a visible report when first observed, before a
-repair can hide them. Record a concise failure, impact, actual process/checkpoint
-state and next action; report material escalation and verified recovery. Use an
-already authorized host notification/scheduler when actually available. Preserve
-pending/unknown/failed/unavailable delivery explicitly and reconcile uncertain
-sends before retrying. Routine negative scientific findings and intentional pause
-are normal states; exhausted resources still need an explicit status report.
